--- !u!114 &1582399053
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1582399051}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 165e79620af194795912fc4f3462b566, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  CyberThreatButtonPrefab: {fileID: 6624401318504971483, guid: 6141ab2add67c4545a0e9d78428eafc5, type: 3}
  EnemyName: {fileID: 1120943276}
  EnemyDescription: {fileID: 625691097}
  EnemyImage: {fileID: 675882661}
  enemies:
  - enemySprite: {fileID: 3961157338269725724, guid: c008ebeb1ad8fee4ab39421ca679cabb, type: 3}
    enemyName: Worm
    enemyDescription: A worm is a bad computer program that makes copies of itself
      and spreads to other computers. It can get into your computer by finding a
      weakness or by tricking people into clicking on links in emails or text messages.
      Once it's in, it can mess up files, add more bad programs, or keep spreading
      until the computer is too full to work.
    enemyLink: N/A
  - enemySprite: {fileID: 8056051307728902024, guid: 2421ccefdfcfad14f960f33fe8f0328c, type: 3}
    enemyName: Virus
    enemyDescription: 'A virus is a bad computer program that attaches itself to
      other programs or files. It spreads when you open or share those files. A virus
      can mess up your computer, make it run slow, or even delete important stuff.
      It can spread to other computers when you share infected files or programs
      with others.         '
    enemyLink: N/A
  - enemySprite: {fileID: 7877142841118543673, guid: 83f3ba74f45e64f44a31410798b63256, type: 3}
    enemyName: DoS
    enemyDescription: "A Denial-of-Service (DoS) attack is when a bad person sends
      too many fake requests to a network, making it hard for normal users to do
      things like check email, visit websites, or use online accounts. It doesn\u2019t
      usually cause data loss, but it can waste a lot of time and money trying to
      fix the problem."
    enemyLink: N/A
  - enemySprite: {fileID: 7028234744703695487, guid: 69978410a0f2a5b4cbf2d672ea6a26b2, type: 3}
    enemyName: DDoS
    enemyDescription: Like DoS, but DDoS comes from many computers. DDoS attacks
      are harder to stop because there are more computers involved in the attack.
    enemyLink: N/A
  - enemySprite: {fileID: 1423351319076176629, guid: 005baec26f367f346a72a24c67cb41b5, type: 3}
    enemyName: Sus Email
    enemyDescription: 'Email spoofing is when a bad person sends an email that looks
      like it''s from someone you trust, like a business or friend. Because the email
      looks real, you might open it and click on a dangerous link or download a harmful
      attachment. This can trick people into giving away sensitive information or
      letting in a virus.         '
    enemyLink: N/A
  - enemySprite: {fileID: -3607382416444627070, guid: c64d6201cdefcca46bcdf7256614ac2e, type: 3}
    enemyName: Sus Call
    enemyDescription: Suspicious Call, when people send fake calls to trick you into
      giving away personal information like passwords, usernames, or credit card
      numbers. They might pretend to be your bank or a shipping company to make you
      believe the call is real!
    enemyLink: N/A
  - enemySprite: {fileID: 1846768129006060653, guid: 87e5c384678eb7b42ba7615c38f0a60c, type: 3}
    enemyName: Sus Text
    enemyDescription: 'Smishing is when bad people send fake text messages to trick
      you into giving away personal information like passwords, usernames, or credit
      card numbers. They might pretend to be your bank or a shipping company to make
      you believe the message is real.         '
    enemyLink: N/A
  - enemySprite: {fileID: 6708131182710439075, guid: ad7405a73e74d81438cf4ecefdd19024, type: 3}
    enemyName: Cryptojacking
    enemyDescription: Cryptojacking is when someone secretly uses your computer to
      mine cryptocurrency without your permission. This usually happens through malware,
      which is bad software that can get onto your computer by tricking you into
      clicking on bad links or visiting infected websites. Sometimes, it can also
      happen through ads or websites that run code on your computer while you're
      browsing.
    enemyLink: N/A
  - enemySprite: {fileID: 1965859600184778311, guid: 1e22c4810a0dc2049a1e4ba2d0cff493, type: 3}
    enemyName: Trojan
    enemyDescription: A Trojan is a type of bad software that looks like a normal
      program or file, such as something you might download for free. It tricks you
      into thinking it's safe, but once installed, it can cause harm. Trojans are
      often spread through tricks like phishing or fake websites.
    enemyLink: N/A
  - enemySprite: {fileID: 2580976388470836715, guid: e514452473057ed40acf788fc55f94e1, type: 3}
    enemyName: Ransomware
    enemyDescription: 'In a ransomware attack, a bad person locks up your files with
      special encryption and demands money to unlock them. They usually trick you
      into clicking on a dangerous link in a phishing email, but they can also use
      security holes in software or mistakes in settings to get in. If you don''t
      pay, you might lose access to your files.         '
    enemyLink: N/A
